				<r3d:repositoryUrl>https://cdha.wisc.edu/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The CDHA assists researchers to create, document, and distribute public use microdata on health and aging for secondary analysis.  Major research themes include: midlife development and aging; economics of population aging; inequalities in health and aging; international comparative studies of health and aging; and the investigation of linkages between social-demographic and biomedical research in population aging.  The CDHA is one of fourteen demography centers on aging sponsored by the National Institute on Aging.</r3d:description>
